## Non-Functional Requirements

### REQ-014: Performance

targets:
  - API response time P95: < 100ms
  - Kafka event latency end-to-end: < 50ms
  - Frontend load time (LCP): < 2.5s
  - Database query time P95: < 50ms
  - Support 10,000 tasks per user without degradation
  - Handle 1,000 concurrent users

---

### REQ-015: Scalability

targets:
  - Horizontal scaling: 2-10 pods per service
  - Database connection pooling: 20 connections per service
  - Kafka throughput: 1,000 events/second
  - Redis cache hit rate: > 80%

---

### REQ-016: Reliability

targets:
  - Service uptime: 99.9% (< 43 minutes downtime/month)
  - Data durability: 99.999999999% (11 nines via cloud provider)
  - Automated failover: < 60 seconds
  - Backup and restore: daily backups, 30-day retention

---

## Acceptance Criteria for Phase V Completion

phase_complete_when:
  - ✅ All Part A features implemented and tested
  - ✅ Minikube deployment working (Part B)
  - ✅ Cloud deployment to AKS/GKE/OKE (Part C)
  - ✅ CI/CD pipeline operational
  - ✅ Monitoring and logging configured
  - ✅ Load tests passing (1,000 concurrent users)
  - ✅ E2E tests passing
  - ✅ Documentation complete (README, API docs, architecture diagrams)
  - ✅ Zero critical bugs
  - ✅ Security audit passed

---

## Out of Scope (Future Phases)

not_in_phase_v:
  - Mobile apps (iOS, Android)
  - Email/SMS notifications (only in-app for now)
  - Multi-tenancy / team workspaces
  - Third-party integrations (Google Calendar, Slack, etc.)
  - Advanced analytics dashboard
  - Task templates
  - Subtasks / hierarchical tasks
  - File attachments

---

## Dependencies

external_dependencies:
  - OpenAI API (for chat agent)
  - Neon PostgreSQL (managed database)
  - Confluent Cloud or Redpanda Cloud (managed Kafka) - for cloud deployment
  - Cloud provider account (Azure, GCP, or Oracle Cloud)
  - GitHub Actions (CI/CD)

---

## Risks and Mitigations

risks:
  - risk_id: RISK-001
    description: "Kafka event ordering issues"
    impact: "High - duplicate tasks or missed events"
    mitigation: "Use single partition per user_id for ordered events"

  - risk_id: RISK-002
    description: "Dapr learning curve"
    impact: "Medium - slower development"
    mitigation: "Start with simple building blocks (Pub/Sub), expand gradually"

  - risk_id: RISK-003
    description: "Cloud cost overruns"
    impact: "Medium - budget concerns"
    mitigation: "Set up billing alerts, use spot instances for non-production"

  - risk_id: RISK-004
    description: "Database migration failures"
    impact: "High - data loss or downtime"
    mitigation: "Test migrations on staging, have rollback plan"

